    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper, so `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners`: when a create repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the endpoint replays the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in `AGENTS.md`, I added:\n\n**New Spring bean** (`rest/support/IdempotencyStore.java`) \u2014 a process-local `ConcurrentHashMap` mapping seen key \u2192 created owner id, injected into functions by type.\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyKeys` \u2014 reads the optional header directly off `ServerHttpConnection` so an absent header is simply `null` rather than a binding failure.\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new first step; uses two `@Flow` outputs: `existing` (key already seen \u2192 replay) and `proceed` (fresh create \u2192 normal pipeline). It reads only the header, never the body, so `ValidateOwnerRequiredFields` stays the sole `@RequestBody` binder.\n- `RespondWithExistingOwner` \u2014 loads the original owner by the id handed over as `@Parameter` and responds 200 with `OwnerDto`.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 after `SaveOwner` (id assigned), records the key \u2192 owner id when a key is present.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`):\n- `checkIdempotency` prepended as entry point with `outputs: { existing: respondExisting, proceed: validate }`.\n- `respondExisting` added under `readonly-transaction` governance.\n- `recordIdempotency` inserted between `save` and `audit`, under the write transaction.\n\nRequests without the header flow through the unchanged create path, so all existing behavior is preserved.",
