    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything `POST /api/owners` does, top to bottom through the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` guards the whole endpoint. Without that role \u2192 denied.\n\n## 1. `CheckIdempotencyKey` (side-effect: branch)\nReads the `Idempotency-Key` header only (never the body). If the key was already recorded for a prior successful create, it branches to `RespondWithExistingOwner` (a 200 replay). Otherwise it proceeds down the create pipeline.\n\n- **`RespondWithExistingOwner`** (replay branch only, read-only tx): loads the originally-created owner by id and responds **200** with it; throws `NotFoundException` if that owner is gone. *(Not on the normal create path.)*\n\n## 2. `ValidateOwnerRequiredFields` \u2014 the only `@RequestBody` step\n- **Side-effect:** normalizes the address in place. Composes `address` from structured `addressLine1` (+ optional `addressLine2`), preferring structured fields and falling back to the flat `address`; writes normalized `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and composed `address` back onto the DTO.\n- **Validation:** rejects (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, reported as an `errors` array) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (composed), `city`, `telephone` is null/blank.\n- **Side-effect:** republishes the validated DTO as a variable for later steps.\n\n## 3. `ValidateRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation:** if `registrationDate` is supplied and is after the server's current date \u2192 reject (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). Omitted date is allowed.\n\n## 4. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`\n- **Side-effect:** rewrites `telephone` to E.164 form in place.\n- **Validation:** anything that can't form a valid number \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n\n## 5. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`\n- Email optional: null/blank \u2192 left untouched.\n- **Validation:** if present, must match the email regex, else **400** (`InvalidEmailException`).\n- **Side-effect:** stores the trimmed, lower-cased email back on the DTO.\n\n## 6. `ValidateOwnerEmailDomain`\n- Optional: absent email \u2192 no-op.\n- **Validation:** if the domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400** (`DisposableEmailDomainException`).\n\n## 7. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`\n- Optional: null/blank \u2192 no-op.\n- **Validation:** must be exactly four digits, and (for a city with a known region) fall within that region's range, else **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Value left unchanged.\n\n## 8. `EnsureUniqueIdentity`\n- **Validation:** computes a household id `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`; if it matches any non-soft-deleted existing owner \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerException`). `sharesHousehold = true` bypasses this check.\n\n## 9. `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- **Validation:** counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 **50** \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n## 10. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`\n- **Validation:** rolls the effective registration date forward to a business day; counts existing owners with that registration date; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 **429** (`TooManyOwnersTodayException`).\n\n---\n*From here the write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`) spans every remaining step; it commits once at the end.*\n\n## 11. `BuildOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** maps the validated DTO into a new `Owner` entity (published as a variable).\n\n## 12. `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized last name + postcode.\n\n## 13. `AssignHouseholdSize`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing that `householdId`, plus 1 for this new owner.\n\n## 14. `ApplyRegistrationDate`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or server date if none), rolled forward past weekends/public holidays to a business day.\n\n## 15. `AssignCustomerCode`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over E.164 telephone + last name), de-duplicated with `-<n>` (n \u2265 2) if it collides with an existing code.\n\n## 16. `AssignMembershipNumber`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year (1 July basis) of the adjusted registration date.\n\n## 17. `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = count of pre-existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## 18. `AssignMembershipLevel`\n- **Side-effect:** computes `membershipPoints` (+2 email present, +1 no namesakes, +2 household \u2265 3, +3 tenure > 1 fiscal year) and derives `membershipLevel` (1: 0\u20131 pts, 2: 2\u20133, 3: 4\u20135, 4: 6+).\n\n## 19. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than **80** owners already exist for this owner's business day.\n\n## 20. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. Defaults false; if a non-deleted existing owner shares the normalized last name + postcode but has a *different* telephone, flags `possibleDuplicate = true` and records that owner's id. Skipped (stays false) when `sharesHousehold = true` or no postcode.\n\n## 21. `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persists the owner (id assigned).\n\n## 22. `RecordIdempotencyKey`\n- **Side-effect:** if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id for future replay.\n\n## 23. `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** emits an `AUDIT` log line with the owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n## 24. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the `OwnerDto` body. Transaction commits.\n\n---\n\nA couple of things worth flagging, since they affect how you'd read the above:\n\n- **Errors thrown by any step** are handled by the matching YAML in `officefloor/escalation/` (e.g. `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, `DuplicateOwnerException`, etc.), most-specific-first, rather than by `@ControllerAdvice`.\n- The three `Ensure*` validations (**9/10/11 above \u2014 unique identity, city capacity, daily limit**) each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and run *before* the transaction opens, so they're a read snapshot, not a locked check \u2014 concurrent creates could each pass and then both commit.\n\nI read the code without changing anything, as requested."
  },
